      "slug": "independence-or-death",
      "title": "Independence or Death",
      "year": 1888,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7e/Pedro_Am%C3%A9rico_-_Independ%C3%AAncia_ou_Morte_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 34130,
      "imageHeight": 18254,
      "story": "The 1888 painting Independence or Death, also known as the Cry of Ipiranga is an oil on canvas painting by Pedro Américo, from 1888. It is the best known artwork representing the proclamation of the Brazilian independence.",
      "facts": [
        "The Brazilian imperial house commissioned the work, due to investments into the construction of the Museu do Ipiranga (presently the Museu Paulista).",
        "A study with children has shown that in part due to the influence of the illustrations in didactic books, they represented the act of independence inspired by the graphical reference of Independência ou Morte.",
        "The work was digitalised as a gigapixel image with Google's Art Camera, to record details in the work that are imperceptible to the naked eye.",
        "Independência ou Morte is the largest painting to be digitalised by Google in Brazil."
      ],
